WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.333 --> 00:00:08.366
Hi. My name

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:09.766
is Adam Cohen. I am a professor

00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:11.266
in the Departments of Chemistry

00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:12.432
and Physics at Harvard.

00:00:12.433 --> 00:00:13.632
Today I am going to talk

00:00:13.633 --> 00:00:14.499
to you about

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.666
a huge unsolved problem

00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:18.632
of how to visualize electrical activity

00:00:18.633 --> 00:00:20.232
in the brain.

00:00:20.233 --> 00:00:21.566
Now take a minute

00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:22.099
and put your hand

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:23.132
on your head

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:24.166
and think about what you are touching.

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:26.899
Within a centimeter of your fingers

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:29.099
there is a piece of the most mysterious

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:30.532
and poorly understood matter

00:00:30.533 --> 00:00:31.666
in the universe.

00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:34.132
Here is a picture of your brain.

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:35.399
Now if we zoom in

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.232
by a factor of about 300

00:00:37.233 --> 00:00:39.266
we see that this brain

00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:40.932
is made up of neurons.

00:00:40.933 --> 00:00:43.166
There is about a hundred billion of them,

00:00:43.167 --> 00:00:44.266
and they are connected

00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:45.599
to each other each by

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:46.566
about ten to the fourth,

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:48.232
10,000 connections.

00:00:48.233 --> 00:00:49.899
If we zoom in again,

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.899
now by a factor of 10,000,

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.566
we see that each one

00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:54.899
of these neurons is encased

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.166
in a lipid bilayer,

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:57.766
a little layer of grease,

00:00:57.767 --> 00:00:59.832
which separates the inside of the cell

00:00:59.833 --> 00:01:01.166
from the outside of the cell.

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:03.732
This bilayer is an electrical insulator

00:01:03.733 --> 00:01:04.632
while the cytoplasm

00:01:04.633 --> 00:01:05.999
and the extracellular medium

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.199
are conductors.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:07.899
So you can think of it

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.266
a little bit like

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:11.432
a parallel plate capacitor.

00:01:11.433 --> 00:01:13.766
Now there are many proteins

00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:14.999
that sit in the membrane

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.399
and these proteins

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.432
can pass ions

00:01:18.433 --> 00:01:19.466
across the membrane.

00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:20.566
There are charge pumps,

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:22.066
which can generate a voltage,

00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:23.332
and there are ion channels,

00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:24.499
which can relieve this voltage.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:25.966
These channels act

00:01:25.967 --> 00:01:26.832
a little bit like resistors

00:01:26.833 --> 00:01:29.299
except that they are non linear, so if

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.499
there is a change in the voltage,

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:31.366
they can have big changes

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:32.166
in the conductance

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:33.499
which can lead to these

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:34.432
electrical spikes

00:01:34.433 --> 00:01:35.332
in the membrane voltage,

00:01:35.333 --> 00:01:36.132
which we call

00:01:36.133 --> 00:01:36.932
action potentials.

00:01:36.933 --> 00:01:38.766
Every action potential

00:01:38.767 --> 00:01:40.399
is about a tenth of a volt high

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.166
and lasts about

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.566
one one-thousandth of a second.

00:01:42.567 --> 00:01:43.966
These are the currency

00:01:43.967 --> 00:01:45.499
of the nervous system.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:46.566
So every thought

00:01:46.567 --> 00:01:48.099
and hope and dream

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:49.232
and feeling that we have

00:01:49.233 --> 00:01:51.566
is encoded in these patterns

00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:52.466
of electrical spikes

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:53.732
traveling through the

00:01:53.733 --> 00:01:54.566
hundred billion neurons

00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:55.099
in our brain.

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:56.732
That is all there is.

00:01:56.733 --> 00:01:57.799
And so we'd really like

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:59.666
to see these action potentials

00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:01.332
so that we can understand

00:02:01.333 --> 00:02:02.999
what each neuron is doing

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:03.966
and also to look at

00:02:03.967 --> 00:02:05.999
the global patterns of activity

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:06.766
and the interrelations

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:07.632
of the signals between 

00:02:07.633 --> 00:02:08.932
neurons to understand

00:02:08.933 --> 00:02:09.799
how information

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:10.699
is being processed

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:12.132
within the nervous system.

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:14.832
So, basically this is a

00:02:14.833 --> 00:02:15.766
voltage measurement problem.

00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:18.632
Now traditionally this is measured,

00:02:18.633 --> 00:02:18.966
as you might

00:02:18.967 --> 00:02:19.966
measure the voltage

00:02:19.967 --> 00:02:20.999
in any electrical circuit.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.699
Electrophysiologists take a glass pipette

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:26.632
with a little electrode in it

00:02:26.633 --> 00:02:27.432
and jam the pipette

00:02:27.433 --> 00:02:28.899
into a cell and then there is

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:29.599
another electrode

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:31.366
out in the solution

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:31.799
and by hooking these up

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:32.432
to an amplifier

00:02:32.433 --> 00:02:33.366
they can measure

00:02:33.367 --> 00:02:34.299
the voltage difference.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:35.232
And this works nicely,

00:02:35.233 --> 00:02:36.566
but it only measures

00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:38.666
one cell at a time.

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:40.099
It's extremely slow

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.399
and laborious to get these

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.766
electrodes into the cell,

00:02:42.767 --> 00:02:44.199
and it doesn't give

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:45.799
you the global view of

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:46.632
what is going on in

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:48.599
a complex neural circuit.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.799
Here is an artist's conception

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:51.866
of what we would really

00:02:51.867 --> 00:02:52.266
like to do.

00:02:52.267 --> 00:02:53.599
We'd like to just make these

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:55.766
neurons light up when they fire.

00:02:55.767 --> 00:02:56.866
The problem is

00:02:56.867 --> 00:02:57.832
that you can't see

00:02:57.833 --> 00:02:59.499
the voltage in a neuron

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:00.932
anymore than you can see

00:03:00.933 --> 00:03:02.366
the voltage in a telephone cord

00:03:02.367 --> 00:03:03.566
when somebody is having

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:04.566
a telephone conversation.

00:03:04.567 --> 00:03:05.732
We need some

00:03:05.733 --> 00:03:07.799
contrast agent to convert

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.799
membrane voltage into light.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:12.199
Now physicists and

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.599
chemists and biologists

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:14.432
have been working on trying

00:03:14.433 --> 00:03:16.299
to invent contrast agent

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:17.432
since the late 1960s.

00:03:17.433 --> 00:03:20.266
And this activity has really taken off

00:03:20.267 --> 00:03:21.899
in the last few years.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:22.532
Here are just a few

00:03:22.533 --> 00:03:23.166
of the things

00:03:23.167 --> 00:03:23.932
that people are working

00:03:23.933 --> 00:03:25.532
on today. These are all from

00:03:25.533 --> 00:03:26.499
within the last year or so.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.766
People are trying to develop

00:03:28.767 --> 00:03:30.066
voltage sensitive dyes.

00:03:30.067 --> 00:03:31.232
So these are organic

00:03:31.233 --> 00:03:32.799
small molecules which will

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:34.932
intercalate into the membrane,

00:03:34.933 --> 00:03:36.332
and in some of these dyes,

00:03:36.333 --> 00:03:38.099
illumination with light

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.566
generates an electronic excited state.

00:03:40.567 --> 00:03:42.099
The charge distribution

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:43.332
in the excited state

00:03:43.333 --> 00:03:44.599
is different than the

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:45.666
charge distribution in the ground state,

00:03:45.667 --> 00:03:47.132
and so when there is a voltage

00:03:47.133 --> 00:03:47.832
across the membrane

00:03:47.833 --> 00:03:49.866
that voltage perturbs

00:03:49.867 --> 00:03:51.166
the relative energy

00:03:51.167 --> 00:03:51.966
of these two states

00:03:51.967 --> 00:03:52.832
which can alter

00:03:52.833 --> 00:03:53.799
the fluorescence properties

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:54.899
of the dye.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:55.732
And so, this provides

00:03:55.733 --> 00:03:56.599
a means to read out

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:57.532
membrane voltage with

00:03:57.533 --> 00:03:58.399
fluorescence.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:03:59.966
Other people are trying

00:03:59.967 --> 00:04:00.999
to put semiconductor

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.399
nanocrystals

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:03.432
in lipid membranes.

00:04:03.433 --> 00:04:05.099
These nanocrystals have

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.266
quantum-mechanical,

00:04:06.267 --> 00:04:08.132
delocalized electronic states.

00:04:08.133 --> 00:04:09.466
Membrane voltage can again

00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:10.766
shift the relative energies

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:11.999
of these states

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.199
and adjust again the

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:13.966
fluorescent properties

00:04:13.967 --> 00:04:15.066
of these crystals.

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:16.699
Other people are working

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:17.999
with objects called

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.799
nitrogen vacancies in diamonds.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.666
These are tiny quantum

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:22.732
mechanical defects

00:04:22.733 --> 00:04:23.766
in diamonds

00:04:23.767 --> 00:04:25.199
and people think that if you

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.099
get a small enough

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.799
diamond nanocrystal

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.732
and you stick it into a membrane

00:04:29.733 --> 00:04:30.932
the fluorescent properties

00:04:30.933 --> 00:04:32.232
of these nitrogen vacancies

00:04:32.233 --> 00:04:33.366
will again be sensitive

00:04:33.367 --> 00:04:34.166
to membrane voltage.

00:04:34.167 --> 00:04:35.999
Now I want to emphasize

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.866
these are all interesting

00:04:37.867 --> 00:04:39.066
prospective technologies,

00:04:39.067 --> 00:04:40.066
but none of these

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:41.066
have solved the problem

00:04:41.067 --> 00:04:42.632
that I posed at the beginning yet.

00:04:42.633 --> 00:04:45.266
In all of these technologies

00:04:45.267 --> 00:04:47.132
the sensor is sitting

00:04:47.133 --> 00:04:47.766
in the membrane.

00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:48.866
And this is because

00:04:48.867 --> 00:04:49.866
to measure a voltage difference,

00:04:49.867 --> 00:04:50.866
you need to be connected

00:04:50.867 --> 00:04:52.332
both to the inside of the cell

00:04:52.333 --> 00:04:53.299
and the outside of the cell.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:56.166
Other people, including myself,

00:04:56.167 --> 00:04:59.299
are working on voltage indicators

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:00.599
based on fluorescent

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.232
transmembrane proteins.

00:05:02.233 --> 00:05:04.166
The idea is to have a protein

00:05:04.167 --> 00:05:05.432
which sits in a membrane

00:05:05.433 --> 00:05:06.132
and to somehow

00:05:06.133 --> 00:05:07.232
make its fluorescence

00:05:07.233 --> 00:05:08.732
sensitive to the membrane voltage.

00:05:08.733 --> 00:05:09.532
I'll tell you just a

00:05:09.533 --> 00:05:10.466
little bit about one

00:05:10.467 --> 00:05:11.566
indicator which we have been

00:05:11.567 --> 00:05:12.566
developing in my lab.

00:05:12.567 --> 00:05:15.299
The story starts here.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.366
This is a picture of the Dead Sea.

00:05:17.367 --> 00:05:19.632
There is a micro-organism that lives

00:05:19.633 --> 00:05:21.699
in the water here that produces

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:22.932
a transmembrane protein

00:05:22.933 --> 00:05:24.566
called archaerhodopsin-3.

00:05:24.567 --> 00:05:27.266
This protein absorbs sunlight

00:05:27.267 --> 00:05:29.166
and uses that energy

00:05:29.167 --> 00:05:30.566
to pump a proton, a charge,

00:05:30.567 --> 00:05:31.799
from inside the cell

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:32.966
to outside the cell.

00:05:32.967 --> 00:05:35.532
This generates a membrane voltage,

00:05:35.533 --> 00:05:36.066
which this creature uses

00:05:36.067 --> 00:05:37.332
to power its metabolism.

00:05:37.333 --> 00:05:39.799
So a few years ago

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:40.632
I said to myself

00:05:40.633 --> 00:05:41.432
I wonder if we

00:05:41.433 --> 00:05:42.332
can run this thing

00:05:42.333 --> 00:05:43.232
in reverse.

00:05:43.233 --> 00:05:44.866
Can we use a change

00:05:44.867 --> 00:05:46.066
in membrane voltage

00:05:46.067 --> 00:05:47.732
to induce a conformational

00:05:47.733 --> 00:05:48.732
change in this protein

00:05:48.733 --> 00:05:50.999
which will lead to a fluorescence

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.066
signal that we can see?

00:05:52.067 --> 00:05:54.499
Just like this. Right.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:55.666
And you see this works

00:05:55.667 --> 00:05:56.199
in Powerpoint,

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:56.799
so that is very encouraging.

00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:58.932
After several years

00:05:58.933 --> 00:05:59.366
we engineered

00:05:59.367 --> 00:05:59.999
a protein which

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:00.699
had these attributes.

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:03.599
And here is a picture

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.532
of a human tumor cell

00:06:05.533 --> 00:06:06.499
where we have introduced

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:08.466
a gene for this protein

00:06:08.467 --> 00:06:11.299
and we are using a little patch pipette,

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:11.832
which you can't see,

00:06:11.833 --> 00:06:13.699
to induce steps of voltage

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:14.466
between plus and minus

00:06:14.467 --> 00:06:15.632
a tenth of a volt,

00:06:15.633 --> 00:06:16.632
and we are looking at the fluorescence

00:06:16.633 --> 00:06:18.566
of the protein.

00:06:18.567 --> 00:06:20.499
So here you can see

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:21.766
that as the voltage goes up,

00:06:21.767 --> 00:06:22.699
the protein gets bright,

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:23.966
and as the voltage goes down

00:06:23.967 --> 00:06:25.199
the protein gets dim.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:26.166
So this is a

00:06:26.167 --> 00:06:27.932
genetically encoded fluorescent

00:06:27.933 --> 00:06:29.166
reporter of membrane voltage,

00:06:29.167 --> 00:06:30.099
and it turns out

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:30.932
that it can be quite fast

00:06:30.933 --> 00:06:31.699
and sensitive

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:32.799
but also very dim,

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:34.566
which makes it hard to measure.

00:06:34.567 --> 00:06:35.899
We have now developed technology

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:37.266
to take these proteins

00:06:37.267 --> 00:06:38.899
and to express them

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:40.566
in neurons in a Petri dish.

00:06:40.567 --> 00:06:42.132
So the neurons become fluorescent

00:06:42.133 --> 00:06:43.232
and their fluorescence

00:06:43.233 --> 00:06:44.166
becomes sensitive

00:06:44.167 --> 00:06:44.899
to the voltage

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:45.166
in the membrane.

00:06:45.167 --> 00:06:46.699
We are also expressing

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:49.566
another protein in these cells

00:06:49.567 --> 00:06:50.366
which renders them

00:06:50.367 --> 00:06:52.566
sensitive to blue light.

00:06:52.567 --> 00:06:53.799
This is a light gated

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:54.832
ion channel

00:06:54.833 --> 00:06:56.366
and targeting a

00:06:56.367 --> 00:06:57.232
flash of blue light

00:06:57.233 --> 00:06:57.732
to the cell body

00:06:57.733 --> 00:06:58.832
will trigger the

00:06:58.833 --> 00:06:59.799
neuron to fire.

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:00.999
We have developed

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:02.232
computational techniques

00:07:02.233 --> 00:07:04.099
to infer the propagation

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:05.832
of these electrical impulses

00:07:05.833 --> 00:07:08.032
at an extremely high time resolution.

00:07:08.033 --> 00:07:09.299
Here I will show you a movie

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:10.499
at a one hundred thousand

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:11.466
frames per second

00:07:11.467 --> 00:07:13.032
of this optically induced

00:07:13.033 --> 00:07:14.066
action potential

00:07:14.067 --> 00:07:15.332
propagating through a neuron.

00:07:15.333 --> 00:07:18.566
And you can really see

00:07:18.567 --> 00:07:19.499
how these signals

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:21.266
propagate through a cell now,

00:07:21.267 --> 00:07:24.099
but this is a neuron in culture.

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:24.666
We have taken a rat brain

00:07:24.667 --> 00:07:25.632
and we've mushed it up

00:07:25.633 --> 00:07:26.466
and we spread out

00:07:26.467 --> 00:07:27.699
the neurons in a dish.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:29.366
We'd really like to do this

00:07:29.367 --> 00:07:30.999
in an intact brain,

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:31.699
but neither we

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:32.999
nor anybody else on the planet

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:34.732
knows how to do that right now.

00:07:34.733 --> 00:07:36.699
There are several challenges to this,

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:37.832
and I'll tell you about them.

00:07:37.833 --> 00:07:41.899
So one of the

00:07:41.900 --> 00:07:42.866
problems we face

00:07:42.867 --> 00:07:44.232
is that the brain

00:07:44.233 --> 00:07:45.699
is not transparent.

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:46.666
Here is a picture

00:07:46.667 --> 00:07:48.766
of a mouse brain.

00:07:48.767 --> 00:07:50.066
And you can see

00:07:50.067 --> 00:07:51.699
that it scatters light

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:52.066
very strongly.

00:07:52.067 --> 00:07:54.499
It's about the size of my pinky

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:54.932
but light scatters

00:07:54.933 --> 00:07:55.766
over a distance of

00:07:55.767 --> 00:07:57.232
less than a tenth of a millimeter.

00:07:57.233 --> 00:07:58.932
And so it is an

00:07:58.933 --> 00:08:00.199
unsolved challenge how to

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:01.832
visualize what is going on

00:08:01.833 --> 00:08:03.799
inside of this chunk of tissue.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:05.032
We need to come up with new kinds

00:08:05.033 --> 00:08:07.466
of optical or electrical tricks.

00:08:07.467 --> 00:08:08.999
Another challenge

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:10.232
is that in every

00:08:10.233 --> 00:08:11.566
mouse brain there is about

00:08:11.567 --> 00:08:13.066
75 million neurons.

00:08:13.067 --> 00:08:14.666
To record from these

00:08:14.667 --> 00:08:16.099
at a thousand frames per second,

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:17.532
which you need to detect

00:08:17.533 --> 00:08:18.199
action potentials

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:19.166
would lead to a

00:08:19.167 --> 00:08:20.832
data rate of about

00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:22.499
75 gigabytes a second.

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:24.266
We don't know how

00:08:24.267 --> 00:08:25.766
to store this data, let alone

00:08:25.767 --> 00:08:26.699
what to do with it

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:28.066
if we did have it.

00:08:28.067 --> 00:08:29.699
So this brings me to

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:30.999
another unsolved challenge,

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:33.766
which is the interpretation problem.

00:08:33.767 --> 00:08:36.066
So even if we had the best

00:08:36.067 --> 00:08:36.499
technology

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:38.366
imaginable for visualizing

00:08:38.367 --> 00:08:39.866
electrical activity in the brain,

00:08:39.867 --> 00:08:40.799
how do we

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:41.999
interpret it?

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.266
We'd like to relate

00:08:43.267 --> 00:08:45.066
the electrical activity

00:08:45.067 --> 00:08:46.899
to some statement about

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:48.166
the underlying biology

00:08:48.167 --> 00:08:48.666
of the cells.

00:08:48.667 --> 00:08:49.799
What are the ions channels

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:50.632
that are active?

00:08:50.633 --> 00:08:51.232
What's their state

00:08:51.233 --> 00:08:52.166
of regulation?

00:08:52.167 --> 00:08:53.299
What's their distribution?

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:54.566
What's the metabolic

00:08:54.567 --> 00:08:55.866
state of the cell?

00:08:55.867 --> 00:08:56.432
What's happening

00:08:56.433 --> 00:08:57.666
to its energy supply?

00:08:57.667 --> 00:08:58.799
We all experience that

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:00.366
as we go through our

00:09:00.367 --> 00:09:01.799
day to night cycle

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:02.532
the function of our neurons

00:09:02.533 --> 00:09:03.932
changes tremendously,

00:09:03.933 --> 00:09:05.266
whether we are asleep or awake,

00:09:05.267 --> 00:09:06.199
tired or not tired,

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:07.499
hungry or not hungry.

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:08.399
And those changes

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:09.599
are not mediated

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:10.366
by structural changes

00:09:10.367 --> 00:09:11.432
in the brain but

00:09:11.433 --> 00:09:13.199
by changes in presumably

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:14.432
the metabolic state

00:09:14.433 --> 00:09:15.432
of our neurons.

00:09:15.433 --> 00:09:17.299
And then finally we'd like

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:20.066
to infer from patterns of activity

00:09:20.067 --> 00:09:21.699
how the neurons are connected

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:22.399
to each other.

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:23.232
To figure out who is calling

00:09:23.233 --> 00:09:24.232
the shots and

00:09:24.233 --> 00:09:25.066
who is controlling who

00:09:25.067 --> 00:09:25.866
and how they

00:09:25.867 --> 00:09:28.099
integrate and process information.

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:28.932
To illustrate this,

00:09:28.933 --> 00:09:29.766
here is a

00:09:29.767 --> 00:09:31.899
movie of some neurons.

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:32.499
This was a movie

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:33.132
taken in my lab.

00:09:33.133 --> 00:09:34.466
These are neurons in a dish,

00:09:34.467 --> 00:09:35.932
not in an intact brain

00:09:35.933 --> 00:09:36.999
where we will look at

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:37.999
their firing patterns.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:39.366
This is a movie at

00:09:39.367 --> 00:09:39.866
about five hundred

00:09:39.867 --> 00:09:40.499
frames per second.

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:41.266
The neurons have been

00:09:41.267 --> 00:09:42.199
artificially colored

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:43.932
just so you can tell them apart.

00:09:43.933 --> 00:09:45.932
And we can zoom in

00:09:45.933 --> 00:09:47.766
on anyone of these cells.

00:09:47.767 --> 00:09:49.032
and look at its firing pattern,

00:09:49.033 --> 00:09:50.332
and we really don't

00:09:50.333 --> 00:09:51.732
know how to interpret

00:09:51.733 --> 00:09:52.666
these firing patterns

00:09:52.667 --> 00:09:54.466
in terms of the ion channels,

00:09:54.467 --> 00:09:55.399
the energetics,

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:57.766
and the connectivity of these cells.

00:09:57.767 --> 00:10:00.599
So there is tremendous scope

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:01.499
over the coming years

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:03.199
to combine the efforts

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:04.966
of physicists, chemists, and biologists

00:10:04.967 --> 00:10:07.332
to develop technology

00:10:07.333 --> 00:10:08.899
which will let us visualize

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:09.899
the activity

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:12.066
in this little chunk of matter

00:10:12.067 --> 00:10:12.732
that is right between

00:10:12.733 --> 00:10:14.466
all of our ears.

00:10:14.467 --> 00:10:15.100
Thanks.

